Follow mineral and brine inputs through useful chemical grades (@cs-mineral-feeds: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @chemical-supply-systems, #source "../../../chemistry/industrial-chemistry/sources/Ammonia-Acids-Fertilisers-BREF.lingua#r_45NWBJYAMXXSRV071A57EM02GB", #source "../sources/Chemical-Supply-Chain-Profiles-EPA.lingua#r_0E09Q6T7CC9HNWZB3N84E7K21A", #source "../sources/Chemical-Supply-Chains-and-Disruption-Risk-EPA.lingua#r_6Y999Z6S9P5T6FY75NA2HGVW6C", #chemical-supply-systems "../../../chemistry/industrial-chemistry/inorganic/Air-separation-oxygen-nitrogen-and-gas-specification.lingua#r_2WT6DXK7CD9M2VQ1Q8JSC49PS4") { r_3WHQXNXP7EJ36X35N599P0D3XB
**Read:** [Large Volume Inorganic Chemicals — Ammonia, Acids and Fertilisers, BREF LVIC-AAF](../../../chemistry/industrial-chemistry/sources/Ammonia-Acids-Fertilisers-BREF.lingua#r_45NWBJYAMXXSRV071A57EM02GB), complete relevant sulfur/phosphate manufacturing and feed chapters; [Water-treatment chemical supply-chain profiles — EPA](../sources/Chemical-Supply-Chain-Profiles-EPA.lingua#r_0E09Q6T7CC9HNWZB3N84E7K21A), the full sulfuric-acid, phosphate, salt or lime profiles actually chosen; [Understanding Water Treatment Chemical Supply Chains and the Risk of Disruptions — EPA](../sources/Chemical-Supply-Chains-and-Disruption-Risk-EPA.lingua#r_6Y999Z6S9P5T6FY75NA2HGVW6C), the complete precursor and dependency analysis.

Select a salt/brine, a sulfur-bearing source, a phosphate feed and a carbonate/lime product. Connect the mineral or fluid resource, preparation/conversion, impurities and actual users. Keep mass of mineral, mass of saleable chemical and useful active content separate. A mineral name or elemental assay alone does not establish that a feed behaves acceptably in a chosen process.

Use [Mining and mineral engineering — extraction, processing, and continuing work](../../../engineering/mining-and-mineral-engineering/Mining-and-mineral-engineering.lingua#r_22HJPS3RTK5EX1J55YJP75PHYA) and [Metals and metallurgical production — feed, refining, structure, useful products, and recovery](../../metals-and-metallurgical-production/Metals-and-metallurgical-production.lingua#r_59BDAQXT81552YF5F8TH4KQQH1) when extraction, beneficiation or metallurgical co-products determine the chemical supply. Return to the industrial-chemistry acid, alkali and mineral-product methods for the transformation. Here develop the cross-party account: source variability, accepted feed panel, usable grade, storage/transport state and competing destinations.

Construct one source-to-user account with a complete constituent balance and actual documented process information. Compare primary, by-product and recovered sources on the same basis. Identify what must be purified, measured or changed in handling before the substitution is meaningful. Extend the account to operating continuity: the usable source can be limited by a shared mine, plant outage, transport route or another product's demand even when the underlying element is abundant.

**Continue:** [Follow oxygen, nitrogen and other air-derived products through separation and use](../../../chemistry/industrial-chemistry/inorganic/Air-separation-oxygen-nitrogen-and-gas-specification.lingua#r_2WT6DXK7CD9M2VQ1Q8JSC49PS4).

**Return:** [Chemical feedstocks and supply systems — specified materials from origin to accepted use](../Chemical-feedstocks-and-supply-systems.lingua#r_05V6FYWMN0VND552CQE94HHA2Q).
